$DIR/main.p:10:2: cannot pass &Config{...} to atomic.(*Pointer).Store, which keeps it after returning
    A composite literal whose address is taken (at main.p:10) is made in
    reload's frame, as a local variable would be. atomic.(*Pointer).Store passes
    it to StorePointer (types.p:198), which stores it in memory another argument
    points to, so &Config{...} would outlive reload's frame.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Change atomic.(*Pointer).Store to take a value or an owner, which it can
    keep: an owned[T] from new, a shared[T], or a library owner such as a
    vec.Vec.
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3003" for a longer explanation)
